pst-990o: migrate QuackWorks BOSL2 vector-spin calls to the v2.0.747 API and
guard the zero-height oct_prism helper, instead of deleting the modules
(operator ruling on PR #60: fund the tree-wide fix, keep the modules
rendering).

BOSL2 fbcdfdd5 (v2.0.747, PR #1475 ae73c6d) tightened attachable() to assert
is_finite(spin), so every vendored QuackWorks call passing a vector
spin=[x,y,z] aborts with "Invalid spin". For a shape rendered with the
default orient=UP, a vector spin is exactly rotate([x,y,z]) applied around
the whole attachable (BOSL2 built the same rot(spin) transform internally),
so the behaviour-preserving migration is to drop the spin argument and wrap
the call in the equivalent rotation:

  rail(...,  spin=[90,0,0],  anchor=FRONT)   -> xrot(90) rail(..., anchor=FRONT)
  multiconnectSlot(..., spin=[90,0,0])       -> xrot(90) multiconnectSlot(...)
  cyl(...,   spin=([90,0,180]))              -> rot([90,0,180]) cyl(...)
  cuboid(..., spin=[t?0:90,0,0]){...}        -> rot([t?0:90,0,0]) cuboid(...){...}

For offset_sweep used as an attach() child, the vector spin runs through
_attach_transform's $attach_to branch; working that transform through,
spin=[0,270,0] there is equivalent to an outer yrot(90) on the (spin=0)
attach child, verified geometry-identical (Δvolume = 0):

  attach(...) ... offset_sweep(..., spin=[0,270,0]) -> attach(...) ... yrot(90) offset_sweep(...)

The GeneratePart(...) call in UnderwareShelf also passed spin=[90,90,0], but
GeneratePart has no spin parameter so that argument was always inert; it is
dropped.

Two further v2.0.747 tightenings surface once the spins render again, both
fixed here behaviour-preservingly (verified geometry-identical against the
456fcd8 baseline via trimesh volume/bbox):

  * cylinder(h=0) now asserts h>0. The octagonal-prism helper oct_prism() is
    copy-pasted into four files (Modules/snapConnector.scad,
    Underware/Underware_Connectors.scad, Underware/Underware_keyholes.scad,
    VerticalMountingSeries/InProgress/UnderwareShelf.scad) and is called with
    h=0 at the DOCUMENTED flush-fit setting (Snap_Connector_Height=0 /
    offset=0) — a degenerate no-op section that rendered empty on 456fcd8.
    Every copy's two cylinder emissions are guarded with `if (h > 0)` so the
    flush-fit renders again identically. (Verified: Underware_Connectors and
    Underware_keyholes at Snap_Connector_Height=0 match the 456fcd8 baseline
    volume exactly on the new pin.)

  * attach(..., align=TOP) onto a cone whose top radius is 0 makes the new
    anchor solver (solve_ellipse -> unit()) reject the zero-radius rim with
    "Invalid vector". The Multiconnect slot dimples are r2=0 cones aligned by
    their (zero-radius) tip; giving them r2=0.001 (0.07% of the 1.5mm dimple
    radius, on a subtracted feature) restores a solvable rim with no
    measurable geometry change.

Every touched module renders on 456fcd8 and fbcdfdd5 with identical geometry.
No catalog model uses these BOSL2 modules (the shipped Multiconnect backer is
the BOSL2-free multiconnectSlotDesign.scad, patch 0002), so the model sweep is
unaffected; this patch keeps the README-advertised standalone generators — and
their documented flush-fit setting — rendering under the new pin.

